<title>POLAND: U.S. SEC approves Universal ADR issue.</title>
<headline>U.S. SEC approves Universal ADR issue.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) has given Polish trader Universal SA final approval to issue American Depositary Receipts (ADRs), the company said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>In January the SEC gave Universal the first of two required permits.</p>
<p>The Polish Securities Commission earlier approved the planned issue, to be carried out by the Bank of America, which could amount to up to 9.78 percent of Universal's shares in public trade.</p>
<p>The shares to be sold as ADRs would be taken from those currently on the Warsaw bourse.</p>
<p>Universal currently has 23,100,510 shares outstanding.</p>
<p>Universal's ADR issue would be the fourth by a Polish company following listings by Mostostal Export, Stalexport and Bank Gdanski.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
